# Seeded once by tools/sync.sh into .github/CODEOWNERS, then owned by the
# project. Replace every @ORG/TEAM before this does anything.
#
# This file is half of the Practitioner role's guardrail, and it is the half
# that does nothing on its own.
#
#   CODEOWNERS nominates reviewers. It does not require them.
#
# Until "Require a pull request before merging" and "Require review from Code
# Owners" are both on for the default branch, this file is a suggestion and a
# practitioner with write access can merge their own note. That is the same
# shape ADR 0016 records for the gate: a check that is not required by
# repository settings is a check that passes and blocks nothing. Turn both on,
# then confirm it by trying to merge something without a review.
#
# Get that right and the honest answer to a practitioner's "am I allowed to
# touch this?" becomes yes, permanently, because the repository is what stops
# them rather than their own carefulness.

# Everything needs an engineering review. Start restrictive; widen deliberately.
*                               @ORG/ENGINEERING

# The field-note register. Two owners on purpose.
#
# Engineering is here because a note can become an ADR, a test or a constraint,
# and somebody has to write it. The domain leads are here because the
# disposition obligation in Build DNA's Practitioner role is theirs to notice
# going unmet — a note sitting at `status: new` for a month is visible to
# whoever gets the review request and to nobody else.
/domain/field-notes/            @ORG/ENGINEERING @ORG/DOMAIN-LEADS

# The decision record and the index of what it left open. Maintainer ground:
# an ADR is where a note's argument ends up load-bearing.
/decisions/                     @ORG/ENGINEERING

# The vendored standard. Nothing here is editable in a consuming project —
# check-drift.sh fails the build if it moved — so a pull request touching these
# paths is either a re-sync or a mistake, and both want a maintainer's eyes.
/AGENTS.md                      @ORG/ENGINEERING
/gate/                          @ORG/ENGINEERING
/skills/                        @ORG/ENGINEERING
/rules/                         @ORG/ENGINEERING
/bundle/                        @ORG/ENGINEERING
/.causeway-lock                 @ORG/ENGINEERING
